# acceptance-mutation-manifest-end

# Spec §6.1 (row of Pendientes), with §4.1 (Versión mínima), §5.5 and §5.9. If the
# task is `pendiente` or `atrasada` and has a minimal version, the row shows on
# its own line «Mínima: » followed by the text (complete, not truncated) and the
# button «Hice la mínima». The line is shown even if the task has no first step,
# and below the step line if there is one. It is not shown in `en espera` rows
# (nor postponed nor completed ones) nor in paused ones; this is decided with
# the status at each moment. An `atrasada` task with the checkbox disabled until
# its window opens shows it, with the button disabled. The app does not
# offer it differently depending on how overdue it is or how many times it was done.
# "the task row shows the minimal one" asserts the exact text of the line,
# with its prefix; the queried list has a single row. The style, the text
# button and tapping the line are covered by the QA suite.
# Reference week: Friday 2026-11-13.
Feature: Minimal version in the row

  # Minimal version in the row 1
  # A pendiente task with a minimal version shows it with the prefix «Mínima: »,
  # complete (row 2: long, not truncated), with the button «Hice la mínima»
  # enabled.
  Scenario Outline: Minimal version in the row 1
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the minimal version of the task is <minimal>
    When I query Pendientes at any moment
    Then the task row shows the minimal one <text>
    And the Hice la mínima button of the task is enabled

    Examples:
      | minimal                                                                                                                        | text                                                                                                                                        |
      | Solo el inodoro                                                                                                                | Mínima: Solo el inodoro                                                                                                                     |
      | Abrir el cajón de abajo, sacar solo la ropa blanca y separarla en dos pilas: la que va con agua caliente y la que no se mezcla | Mínima: Abrir el cajón de abajo, sacar solo la ropa blanca y separarla en dos pilas: la que va con agua caliente y la que no se mezcla |

  # Minimal version in the row 2
  # Also in a pendiente relative recurring task.
  Scenario Outline: Minimal version in the row 2
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the minimal version of the task is <minimal>
    When I query Pendientes on <now>
    Then the task row shows the minimal one <text>

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | minimal           | now                 | text                      |
      | 2    | dias   | Solo los helechos | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | Mínima: Solo los helechos |

  # Minimal version in the row 3
  # Also in a pendiente calendar recurring task (on the day of its occurrence).
  Scenario Outline: Minimal version in the row 3
    Given a weekly recurring task on <days> created on <created>
    And the minimal version of the task is <minimal>
    When I query Pendientes on <now>
    Then the task row shows the minimal one <text>

